Date: Wed, 22 Sep 93 12:49:08 PDT
From: tcmay@netcom.com (Timothy C. May)
Subject: Neo-Calvinism--Getting in the Last Word

How best to get in the last word?

Silence.

Being a Neo-Calvinist, I know that the best punishment for
cluelessness is silence. Not only are we not our brother's keeper, but
we have an obligation _not_ to interfere. 

(Neo-Calvinism takes from the Protestant tradition concepts of
salvation and choice, but not concepts of predestination and original
sin. Calvin, and Hobbes, too. Your smileage may vary.)

As an example, the Neo-Calvinist believes that if someone takes
drugs, even to the point of nonfunctioning or facing death, then this
is _their choice_, that interfering with their cluelessness is itself
profoundly immoral.  Interfering with their ability to choose
salvation over sin--I mean these terms metaphorically, but there's a
sense in which I believe they are real states of mind--is itself sin.

(I believe this outlook to be one of the core motivations for
libertarianism, by the way.)

List members on this list and on the Cypherpunks list can confirm that
I rarely have tried to "get in the last word." I did not during the
debate with Eric Raymond over the Pagan Trial (the lead up to it, and
my verdict), and I have not on other matters. I just let threads drop
and often let foolish questions go unanswered. 

(I'm sure I've slipped up at times, and some may interpret things I've
written as attempts to get in the last word. But in general, I favor
silence.)

To the true Calvinist Stoic (another invented term of mine, which I
can explain to anyone interested), nothing is more satisfying than
having an arguer--especially a clueless twerp--keep making points,
ranting on, and being met with silence, golden silence.

An obnoxious paranoid (the worst kind) on the Cypherpunks list is
convinced that I am the anonymous author of some pieces which have
appeared recently. (I am not, for your information.) He posts flames,
snide comments, and he sends me personal notes saying insulting
things. As we do not yet have the "::exclude" capabilities of the
Extropians list, I simply ignore his comments.

In true Neo-Calvinist form, I also take solace in the fact that anyone
who is taken in by specious arguments _deserves_ (a very important
word to Calvinists) to be taken in. Even if the entire Extropians list
were to be taken in by a crummy argument, I'd take solace in this view.

"Correcting the record" is not something I like to do. I also dislike
using those stupid "smileys" to indicate humor. (My account is shared
with Klaus! von Future Prime, who has his own reasons for signing his
posts with this name.)

By now you understand my Neo-Calvinist motivations: those who don't
"get" jokes don't deserve to have them explained. Puns should never be
explained. Irony explained is irony made banal.

Let your tormenters stew in their own juices. When a thread has run
its course, that is, when real information and viewpoints have already
been presented, just let it die. Comfort yourself with the reminder
that your opponent, spewing more "last words" (often with the foolish
line, "this will be my last comment on this thread"),is fooling no
one.

Relish the Calvinist view that no sin goes unpunished.

-Tim

