Date: Wed, 22 Sep 1993 16:33:16 -0400 (EDT)
From: Mark Sulkowski <SULKOM@ubvmsb.cc.buffalo.edu>
Subject: PHIL: Getting over Objectivism

>i thought everyone here was a recovering randian (or are some still in 
>denial?) i also don't want to provoke a debate on whether A=A. reading 
>ayn rand was real mind food. so what now?

	Read different things.  Expand your mind.

	There is quite a mix of people here when it comes to Rand
and Objectivism.  The anti-Objectivism people tend to crowd out those
who have sympathies to it.

	I personally do not consider myself an Objectivist, though I
have (very loosely) called myself a Neo-Objectivist.  (Or, rather,
a supporter of the research activities of Neo-Objectivists.)

	I only started to dig into Objectivism about 2-3 years ago.
So it is still pretty new to me.  I was never convinced by Rand on
a number of issues, though I saw some promise to her philosophy.
I further researched Objectivism, though I made sure to read all
sorts of critiques and alternative ideas from Neo-Objectivists and
non-Objectivists.  That way I have made sure to keep my meme-receptor
sites from getting clogged.

	My impression is that the Neo-Objectivists who are developing
the philosophy have their work cut out for them.  They tend to be
tolerant and open-minded, so there is hope for them yet.  I still
have problems with just about every part of Objectivism.  Maybe their
work will clear some of that up.

	On the other hand, I see promise in the idea that morality
can be objective, though this idea needs major development.  Only
the barest of frameworks exists.  Nothing practical for everyday
living yet, but who knows what the future will bring.

	So I have some sympathy towards Neo-Objectivist research,
though I don't consider myself an "Objectivist".  It is disappointing
to me to see the hostility some people in this list have towards
Objectivism.  Maybe that comes from arguing with Randroids.  I just
hope that everyone (including me, of course) keeps an open mind to
all ideas and their meme-receptors clean and shiny.


